mb|P|mb|P|mb|1C|mb|P|mb|1S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|There is a question as to when you bypass diamonds when responding to 1@C. Many play you always bypass diamonds to bid a 4 card major (hence 1@D denies a major). But there is really no reason to do that. I play the only time you bypass diamonds is if you have 4 diamonds, a 4-card major, and less than an invitational hand. Here North does qualify to bypass diamonds and bid 1@S.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


