https://tinyurl.com/24chycka
qx|A2|st||rh||ah|Board 2 IMPs   -   On January 08, 2024|pn|hondo717,aspiring,amidamin,Honeydog3|
md|4SJ2HT76DK852CK962,S754HQ93D6CAQJT73,SA63HAK842DJT743C,SKQT98HJ5DAQ9C854|sv|n|
mb|1S|mb|P|mb|1N|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I understand why West bid 1N with only 9 HCP because 2@C would establish a game force. Further, I do think West could reevaluate her hand in light of 1@S by partner. |
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Using Bergen Evaluation, West has 9 HCP, 2 length points, 1 point for the quality club suit, and 2 points for the singleton for 14 points, more than enough to make a 2@C game forcing bid.|
PG| ***** 24 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|2s|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2@S by West is a huge underbid. At a minimum West must treat her hand as a 3-card limit raise and bid 3@S. Personally I think 4@S would not be out of line.|
PG| ***** 25 ***** |


ub||
PG| ***** 26 ***** |


mb|3S|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree 100% with the pass. East has a very weak opener, with flat distribution and dubious Jx of hearts. In fact, had West made a 4-card limit raise, although I stretch to bid marginal games with a 9-card fit, I would not bid game even opposite a 4-card limit raise.|
PG| ***** 27 ***** |


