UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Hard hand to play and bid particularly with bad club break. Personally at trick two, after winning the @SK I would have taken the club finesse.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kib: ^*NWould you bid clubs or diamonds as the 2nd bid by opener?|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That is a good question. You can make a case for either. Since the 3 diamonds are much better than the 3 little clubs, 2@D is what I would choose. But often when you have a choice of bids, the lower bid is better as it leaves more room in the auction.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In general with 3-3 in the minors over 1N, you do strain to bid 2@C since that leaves more room in the auction. So that would be reasonable here as well, but 2@D is okay also with this particular deal.

|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


