%%%%%%Hand 3 Hand 3
https://tinyurl.com/293xqm88
qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   On January 08, 2024|pn|hondo717,aspiring,amidamin,Honeydog3|
md|1ST954H4D6532CJ954,SAJ7HKT93DT4CT862,SHJ862DQJ97CAKQ73,SKQ8632HAQ75DAK8C|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|P|mb|1C|mb|D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Normally with even 5 spades and 4 hearts I prefer to bid spades. rather than making a takeout double and here you have 6 spades. However, East is so strong that, should partner bid diamonds or NT, he could double and correct. So the double is better in case partner has hearts.|
PG| ***** 47 ***** |


mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now with 4 clubs and a singleton heart I would normally bid 2@C over the double. Even if you play inverted raises, over a double 2@C is just a weak raise. But my hand is so weak that even 2@C is an overbid.|
PG| ***** 48 ***** |


mb|P|mb|1H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2C?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|When you have a strong distributional hand you can do what I call ^*BPicture Bidding^*n meaning I try to picture reasonable hands for partner to have to decide to bid.|
PG| ***** 49 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|For example, if partner has as little as Kxxxx of hearts 4@H must have good plays. So I would bid 4@H. But 3@H is possible as well if you want to be more conservative. Looking for slam would be a stretch given West has no more than 8 points or so due to lack of jump to 2@H.|
PG| ***** 50 ***** |


mb|4H|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 51 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|CA|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The expert lead from AKQ is the Queen because once it wins, it becomes obvious that North has the @CA and @CK.|
