https://tinyurl.com/2bwkumdc
qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   On January 08, 2024|pn|hondo717,amidamin,aspiring,Honeydog3|
md|3SJT6HQJ832D632C52,SA987H975D987CJ43,S32HAT64DJT54CAQ7,SKQ54HKDAKQCKT986|sv|n|
mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Good pass by North. I really dislike flat 11 point hands. |
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|However, using Bergen evaluation, you could add one point to the North hand because of the 4 aces/tens and only one Queen. That means the hand does meet the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| (12 adjusted Bergen points and 8 cards in the red suits). So you could make a case for opening 1@D, although I like pass better.|
PG| ***** 69 ***** |


mb|1C|mb|P|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|1N|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with the 1N bid by North. Unlike a 1N overcall in direct seat (which is 15-18), a 1N overcall in the pass out seat shows 11-14 or so.|
PG| ***** 70 ***** |


mb|D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2D|an|transfer|
PG| ***** 71 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As I alerted the 2@D is a transfer. Rather than playing systems on over a double of 1N you could play something called ^*BDONT Runouts^*n which I actually prefer.|
PG| ***** 72 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|DONT Runouts are similar in concept to DONT in that a suit by me shows that suit and a higher ranking suit. For example (on a different hand) if I bid 2@D over the double that would show diamonds and a major and redouble shows a single suited hand.|
PG| ***** 73 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With this hand, playing ^*BDONT Runouts^*n I would redouble, partner bids 2@C (pass or correct) and I bid 2@H.|
PG| ***** 74 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3C|mb|P|mb|P|mb|3H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West used |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| and bid 3@H which is okay but risky. West is vulnerable and with all the strength behind her.|
PG| ***** 75 ***** |


 
